{
  "reconstructed_theorem_text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace,BorelSpace and CompleteSpace instances,with canonical ordinary full-space volume;dimension zero is included and no Nontrivial premise is imposed. Let W:E->R be C2 and assume actual volume Integrable exp(-W) and strictly positive volume partition Z=integral exp(-W). Let m,M:R satisfy 0<m<=M. For EVERY x,a:E assume BOTH actual diagonal Frechet-Hessian bounds\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a <= M*||a||^2.\nAdditionally assume actual MemLp id 2 (volume.tilted(-W)):the position-vector identity function is genuinely AE strongly measurable with finite vector L2 norm for this law.\nDefine mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)),the actual normalized Gibbs measure exp(-W)/Z against volume. Then for EVERY a:E,\n  ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin(mu)(a,a) <= ||a||^2/m.\nThe covariance bilinear is the actual dual covariance composed with both Riesz/toDual maps. With the supplied genuine vector second moment and the normalized finite probability law,its diagonal is the true centered projection variance\n  integral <a,x-meanX>^2 dmu(x),where meanX=integral x dmu(x).\nThe explicit position MemLp hypothesis is retained;finite probability alone is not substituted for it. In the API the covariance bilinear outside vector L2 is defined as zero;that fallback is NOT the meaning of this estimate because this premise gives genuine moments. Measure.tilted is the actual withDensity ENNReal.ofReal(exp(h)/integral exp(h)) construction;it is totalized outside normalizable cases,with denominator zero yielding zero density.The explicit integrable positive partition here avoids that normalization fallback.\nThis theorem outputs the single all-direction covariance estimate for this law.It does not output additional operator/kernel/normalized-score identities,anisotropic Hessian-inverse bounds,Hessian regularity of another potential or a whole-paper theorem.Both m/M curvature controls and CompleteSpace are explicit,and all statements retain dimension zero.",
  "reconstructed_text_sha256": "36cf196cfde98133c8233d809d75a7745a0e8ab3c49f985b8c21b328fb8b0880",
